  "verbalization": "Chlorpropamide, a sulfonylurea compound, is linked to Slc22a6 through a shared pathway involving Tolbutamide, a sulfonylurea analog. The evidence suggests that Chlorpropamide and Tolbutamide, both belonging to the class of sulfonylurea antidiabetic agents, bind to Slc22a6. This binding is supported by multiple paths, which highlight a common ancestor in the N-Sulfonylurea category, reinforcing the relationship between the compound and the transporter. The presence of multiple paths with similar scores indicates a consistent mechanism, where the sulfonylurea class plays a central role in the interaction between the drug and Slc22a6. The integration of these pathways suggests that the interaction is not only dependent on the sulfonylurea class but also involves a shared biological mechanism that links the drug to the transporter.",
